WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.010
Two sentences. «Paul aime sa
mère.» Paul loves his mother.

2
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.600
«Léa aime sa mère.» Now
it means her mother.

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.340
Same little word, «sa».

4
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.480
His in one sentence, her in the other.

5
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.150
So how does «sa mère» mean
his mother or her mother?

6
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.880
And how do you know which?

7
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.060
In this mission, you'll
build a grid of words for my,

8
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.110
your, his and her.

9
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.430
Then you'll pick the right
arm of a four-way signpost:

10
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.290
«ce», «cet», «cette» or «ces».

11
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:37.120
Your mission: find out how
«sa» can mean both his and her,

12
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.920
and how to tell whose it is.
